{"name":"After Midnight","hex":"#38393f","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"after","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Behind; later in time; following."]},{"part":"Preposition","definitions":["Subsequently to; following in time; later than.","Subsequently to and as a result of."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/after"},{"term":"midnight","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The middle of the night: the sixth temporal hour, equidistant between sunset and sunrise.","Twelve o'clock at night exactly."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Utterly dark or black."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/midnight"}],"entries":[{"title":"After Midnight (1921 film)","blocks":[{"text":"After Midnight is a lost 1921 American silent drama film directed by Ralph Ince and starring Conway Tearle, Zena Keefe and Warren Black."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/After_Midnight_lobby_card_1921.jpg/330px-After_Midnight_lobby_card_1921.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/After_Midnight_(1921_film)"},{"title":"After Midnight (1927 film)","blocks":[{"text":"After Midnight is a 1927 American silent drama film written and directed by Monta Bell. The film stars are Norma Shearer and Gwen Lee. A copy of After Midnight is housed in the Cinémathèque Française."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/After_Midnight_%281927_film%29.jpg/330px-After_Midnight_%281927_film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/After_Midnight_(1927_film)"},{"title":"After Midnight (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"After Midnight, stylized as @fter midnight or abbreviated @m and alternatively known as After Midnight with Taylor Tomlinson, is an American late-night comedy panel game show hosted by Taylor Tomlinson and executive produced by Stephen Colbert via his company Spartina Productions, Henry R. Muñoz III via his comedy studio Funny or Die, and The Late Show with Stephen Colbert executive producer Tom Purcell. The program premiered on CBS at 12:37 am ET on January 17, 2024, in the time slot previously held by The Late Late Show with next day streaming on Paramount+. It is a reboot of @midnight, which ran from 2013 to 2017 on sister cable network Comedy Central. Upon its debut, it received generally positive reviews."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/After_Midnight_Logo.png/330px-After_Midnight_Logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/After_Midnight_(TV_series)"},{"title":"Midnight","blocks":[{"text":"Midnight is the transition time from one day to the next – the moment when the date changes, on the local official clock time for any particular jurisdiction. By clock time, midnight is the opposite of noon, differing from it by 12 hours."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Tour_de_l%27horloge_de_la_gare_de_Metz_%C3%A0_Minuit_%28juin_2019%29_%28cropped%29.JPG/330px-Tour_de_l%27horloge_de_la_gare_de_Metz_%C3%A0_Minuit_%28juin_2019%29_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midnight"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Midnight_Mist.jpg/500px-Midnight_Mist.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Midnight_Mist.jpg/500px-Midnight_Mist.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Photograph of the moon taken at midnight","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMidnight_Mist.jpg"}],"sounds":{"after":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f4/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhu